\section{Experiment 1: Moderate Congestion}
\label{sec:exp1}

\subsection{Setup}
The Cologne network (79 signalized intersections, 194\,km of road, 9{,}537 passenger trips) was run at demand scale~$0.7$ for 1{,}200\,s per episode. Each strategy controlled 40 of the 79 intersections (ratio~$=0.5$); the rest kept SUMO's default actuated programs. All strategies, including the MARL agent, used \(\Delta t{=}5\)\,s. The MARL checkpoint is \textbf{v8} (\texttt{marl\_cologne\_shared\_dqn\_regionaware\_v8\_scale07.pt}), trained with \(K{=}20\) lane padding. Five strategies were compared---Fixed-Time, SOTL, Adaptive, MaxPressure, and MARL DQN---over 120 episodes each.

\textbf{Seed note.} Due to the way we scheduled runs, each strategy used a different base seed (Fixed-Time: 42, MaxPressure: 142, Adaptive: 242, SOTL: 342, MARL: 42). This means episode-level comparisons are \emph{unpaired}---a limitation we address in Experiment~2 where all strategies share the same seed.

